Aluminium Trihydrate, also known as aluminum trihydroxide or alumina trihydrate, is a white inorganic compound primarily derived from bauxite through the Bayer process. It is widely used as a flame retardant and smoke suppressant in polymers, coatings, adhesives, and other industrial materials.

When exposed to high temperatures, ATH releases chemically bound water, helping cool the material and dilute combustible gases. Its relatively low toxicity and suitability for halogen-free formulations make it an important ingredient in applications where fire safety and environmental considerations influence material selection.

